  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Train that carries my girl from town** (1 review): The opening Train number runs straight into Black Mountain Rag, which the setlist doesn't list [4]\n- **The Coo-Coo Bird** (1 review): Billy plays this one alone in clawhammer banjo style [4]\n- **The Wagoner's Lad** (1 review): Billy also plays this one solo in clawhammer style [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Rolling in My Sweet Baby's arms (sound check)**: back after 42 archived shows (684 days); rare: 6 archived performances [5]\n- **Train that carries my girl from town**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Southbound**: rare: 8 archived performances [5]\n- **Walk on By**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Band Intro's**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **John Henry**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 6 archived performances [5]\n- **Little Sadie**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 11 archived performances [5]\n- **Tom Dooley**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **BSB2017-06-30.BillyStrings2017-06-30a.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 15 songs; 65 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **BSB2017-06-30.BillyStrings2017-06-30.flac16**: source not stated; 15 songs; 65 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Billy tells stories between songs in this set, showing how deeply this music is part of him [3]\n- The set was billed as a High Sierra Playshop titled Shady Grove, devoted to the music of Doc Watson [1]\n- The set was billed as a High Sierra Playshop titled Shady Grove, devoted to the music of Doc Watson [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **BSB2017-06-30.BillyStrings2017-06-30a.flac16**: taped by Jon Hart; transferred by Jon Hart; source: 4 Track [1]. Also: Jon Hart recorded, mixed in Adobe Audition, mastered in Sound Forge, tracked, and uploaded it as FLAC [1]\n- **BSB2017-06-30.BillyStrings2017-06-30.flac16**: taped by Jon Hart; transferred by Jon Hart; source: 4 Track [2]. Also: Jon Hart recorded, mixed in Adobe Audition, mastered in Sound Forge, tracked, and uploaded it as FLAC [2]",
